      "section_name": "Detail Section",
      "section_heading": "Good questions.",
      "heading_level": "h2",
      "eyebrow": "A little more clarity",
      "subheading": "",
      "description": "",
      "paragraphs": [
        "A little more clarity",
        "Whichever you already own: Power BI, Tableau or comparable platforms. The point of this track is making YOUR existing tool earn its license, not selling you a new one.",
        "Data Visualization teaches individuals to build better reports and dashboards. This track is organizational: connecting live data sources, keeping dashboards current, and changing how the team uses them in decisions. They pair well, run in either order.",
        "That staleness is usually an ownership and habit problem, not a tooling one, and it's addressed head-on: who maintains what, refresh workflows, and making the dashboard the meeting's starting point."
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "A little more clarity"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Good questions."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Which BI tools do you train on?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Whichever you already own: Power BI, Tableau or comparable platforms. The point of this track is making YOUR existing tool earn its license, not selling you a new one."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "How is this different from the Data Visualization track?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Data Visualization teaches individuals to build better reports and dashboards. This track is organizational: connecting live data sources, keeping dashboards current, and changing how the team uses them in decisions. They pair well, run in either order."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Our dashboards go stale within months. Does training fix that?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "That staleness is usually an ownership and habit problem, not a tooling one, and it's addressed head-on: who maintains what, refresh workflows, and making the dashboard the meeting's starting point."
        }
